From: "claudio-michel[bot]" <claudio-michel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:03:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway,tools): record plugin-path sends in the delivery
 ledger and return receipts

The gateway's final agent responses get honest at-least-once delivery
through the delivery-obligation ledger (#58818): obligation row before
I/O, attempting/delivered/failed transitions, restart sweep with a
visible recovered marker. Sends made through the send_message tool -
the path plugins and cron use - reached the platform with none of
that: no obligation row, no retry on restart, no receipt, so a crash
between the adapter call and the platform ACK silently lost the
message.

This records the same pending -> attempting -> delivered/failed
transitions around the live-adapter send in _send_via_adapter, behind
the existing gateway.delivery_ledger gate (default on), best-effort at
every step so ledger trouble never blocks or delays a send. The
synthetic session_key carries platform, chat, and thread; the restart
sweep redelivers straight from the row's own fields with the recovered
marker, and its session-resume matching never matches a synthetic key.
Successful sends now additionally return the obligation_id receipt
alongside the existing message_id (additive; absent when the ledger is
gated off).

Consumer: Tether (Parcha-ai/parcha-skills), a Slack-continuation
plugin that must prove to an operator that a reply was durably handed
to the platform.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
